# satellite (galaxy 1) into its real central (galaxy 0), also the FoF central: a minor
# merger, so the black-hole growth's hydrogen cap (M:366-372), the burst's commit caps and
# refresh (M:798-803) and the post-minor-merger recheck (M:806-811) all run.
# Source: R2 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R2/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 c6af6c9385d41adcccbd5f19e064323486706b0965183f61ebded290331f6714), Snap_32 rows 15650 (GalaxyIndex 3000061000000027, Type 0) and 15651 (GalaxyIndex 3000061000000035, Type 1).
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time
# state; the writer stores every galaxy field below verbatim (R/src/io/save_gals_hdf5.c:895-1005;
# DiskScaleRadius is the output's DiskRadius), the bulge radii included.
# Constructed: the galaxies' SnapNum (one less than the row's), deltaMvir (central +2% of
# Mvir, satellite -5%), the clocks (999.9 for the central, B:288; 0.0 for the satellite,
# unread), OutflowRate 0, TimeOfLast*Merger -1 (SAGE26's creation sentinel), zero histories,
# and the call time, dt and bin (the R1 template's: the last bin of the substeps).
# Reachability: R2-reachable.
